<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.Browser.Core.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.8.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.5.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.5.3" />
    <!-- TestUiSession and the form-control tests own their controls through StandardPanel. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Broiler.UI.Panel.Standard" Version="0.1.0-preview.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Broiler.Browser.Core\Broiler.Browser.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    WHAT THIS SUITE STILL TESTS UNDER Debug-VM/Release-VM, NOW THAT THE BRIDGE HAS LEFT.

    The conditional ProjectReference to Broiler.HtmlBridge.Scripting.Vm is gone from here,
    and so are the two files it existed for: VmScriptEngineTests and the JSEAL conformance
    suite's Jseal/VmProviderRegistration.cs both moved to Broiler.HtmlBridge, which is the
    component that owns the engine seam and now runs them itself — 723 cases under
    Release-VM against this repository's 603 under Release.

    THE -VM JOBS HERE ARE STILL WORTH RUNNING, and what they ask is a different question.
    Broiler.Browser.Core reaches the VM script engine under those two build types and
    BrowserApp.NewScriptEngine() picks it with an #if, so these jobs exercise THE BROWSER'S
    OWN HOST CODE — page loading, the render pipeline, the form controls — against an
    engine that is not Broiler.JS. That is an embedder question and it belongs to an
    embedder's suite. Whether the engine answers the contracts is the component's question
    and is asked there.

    The reference itself is not needed for that: this project references
    Broiler.Browser.Core, which carries the conditional reference, so the assembly is in
    the closure under exactly the same configurations it always was.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
